<title>USA: Lear Corp inks joint venture pact in China.</title>
<headline>Lear Corp inks joint venture pact in China.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lear Corp said Thursday it signed a joint venture agreement with Jiangling Motors Co of Nanchang, China.</p>
<p>The partners formed a new company called Lear-Jiangling Interior System Co, which will provide interior automotive parts and services to a Jiangling Motors plant in China. Lear estimated the company will provide seats for 150,000 vehicles annually. Lear and Jiangling will each own a 50-percent stake in the venture in Nanchang, Lear said.</p>
<p>Lear manufactures automotive interior systems, with 135 facilities in 19 countries.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
